@@ -58,6 +58,16 @@ In addition, the `md_globals` parameter of
 `Markdown.extensions.Extension.extendMarkdown()` is no longer recognized as a
 valid parameter and will raise an error if provided.
 
+### The `UnescapePostprocessor` has been deprecated
+
+The `markdown.postprocessors.UnescapePostprocessor` is no longer registered by
+default and now raises a `DeprecationWarning` when instantiated. Backslash
+escaped characters are now restored by the new
+`markdown.treeprocessors.UnescapeTreeprocessor` (registered as `'unescape'`
+with a priority of `0`) before serialization, so that restored characters are
+properly escaped by the serializer. Extensions which relied on escape
+placeholders surviving until the postprocessors should be updated accordingly.
+
 ## New features
 
 The following new features have been included in the 3.4 release:
@@ -97,3 +107,6 @@ The following bug fixes are included in the 3.4 release:
 
 * Extension entry-points are only loaded if needed (#1216).
 * Added additional checks to the `<pre><code>` handling of `PrettifyTreeprocessor` (#1261, #1263).
+* Backslash escaped characters (such as a double quote escaped while using the
+  `smarty` extension) no longer result in invalid HTML when used in attribute
+  values, such as image alt text or link titles.
